checks_run.procedure:
New raw-TCP check (dg2-qa-r11.spec.ts R11-01) against the real built API and PostgreSQL. Over-limit evidence uploads (limit 25 MiB):
(a) the round-10 audit repro: 30 MiB chunked with 'application/octet-stream\t; x=1', one write without backpressure, then the client waits 8 s without closing;
(b) Content-Length 26 MiB, fully sent;
(c) chunked 26 MiB plus terminator;
(d) chunked 25 MiB + 64 KiB, then STALLED (no terminator, client open);
(e) Content-Length 100 MiB declared, 26 MiB sent, then STALLED;
(f) Content-Length 25 MiB + 1, fully sent.
For each case: statuses, Connection header, server FIN/close times, evidence_content rows, stored files, audit rows and the evidence version.

R11-04/05: on ONE keep-alive socket, in order:
- GET /me;
- an upload with an Arabic/emoji/ZWJ file name;
- an upload with a stale If-Match whose small body arrives in one write;
- a JSON note create (Arabic, emoji, ZWJ family, flag, combining marks, RLM) chunked at every UTF-8 continuation byte (72 chunks);
- GET /me again.
Then wait 1 s and compare the API and DB values.

Map the 32 assigned requirements to the suites that ran green in this round:
- p2-journeys Diagnose->G1, Define->G2, Design->G3, charter, T01-T04, TOM canvas/workshop, decisions, evidence review, team roles, EN and AR;
- the integration suites (evidence, record guards, access, contract);
- the unit tests;
- the qa-verifier suites.
